Carol Guensburg examines the ethical[ dile]mmas of news reporting[ that] involve the media agency's[ owner] in the December 1998 issue of American Journalism Review (p. 10). In "When the story is about the owner," she determines that it is up to the individual journalists and news operations to continue[ reporting] important stories, regardless[ of] the impact they may have on corporate or[ advertising interests] (Guensburg,[ p]. 11).
